/* Which legacy prompt format keeps the entry's declared model.
 *
 * Both of them. The store converts an inline entry of either format through
 * the same structured template IR — a Soul entry's `template` is handed over
 * with its own prompt as the instructions instead of being serialised into
 * frontmatter — so `model` survives into `legacy_template` and constrains the
 * conversion the same way in both.
 *
 * Measured as the store's answer twice per row rather than as a value read
 * out of it: once against the profile the entry declares and once against a
 * different one. A row that declares nothing is accepted by both, a row that
 * declares a model is accepted only by its own. */

